model metadata (e.g., old_field.remote_field.through._meta.db_table), which is 
defined by developers in code, not from user input. In standard Django usage, an
attacker cannot control model definitions. The code path is only reachable 
during migrations, which require developer intervention. The prior knowledge 
correctly indicates no SQL injection. The theoretical scenario where an attacker
controls model definitions is unrealistic in typical deployments. Therefore, the
vulnerability is not authentically exploitable.
